      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "The target is the Florida state row for August 2026 in CMS dataset 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c, original submission O, first publication. The ledger does not explicitly name the denominator; this forecast uses CMS's published ex parte rate definition, Metric 5a1 divided by Metric 5, beneficiaries due for renewal. The historical anchors use the same unadjusted initial cohort-outcome variant from each reporting month's snapshot, excluding separately presented updated outcomes."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Evidence limitation: the web tool could not retrieve Florida's raw original rows or the downloadable CSV. HistoricalContext therefore contains fetched official snapshot percentages rounded to whole percentage points, rather than exact one-decimal ratios reconstructed from counts. Exact ex parte numerator counts were not fetched and are not invented."
      },
      {
        "kind": "tool",
        "tool": "official.lookup",
        "call": "Fetch Florida rows in the Coverage Retention and Disenrollment Rates by State tables at https://www.medicaid.gov/resources-for-states/downloads/eligib-oper-and-enrol-snap-sep2025.pdf, https://www.medicaid.gov/resources-for-states/downloads/eligib-oper-and-enrol-snap-oct2025.pdf, https://www.medicaid.gov/resources-for-states/downloads/eligib-oper-and-enrol-snap-nov2025.pdf and https://www.medicaid.gov/resources-for-states/downloads/eligib-oper-and-enrol-snap-dec2025.pdf.",
        "result": "September 2025: 195,239 beneficiaries due, 27% renewed ex parte. October: 192,991 due, 24% ex parte. November: 155,346 due, 24% ex parte. December: 165,970 due, 24% ex parte. Percentages use beneficiaries due as denominator."
